# Left-aligned website text

- Left-align text by default in all new and edited website experiences, including headings, body copy, helper text, notices, forms, carts, and empty states.
- Use `text-left` where a parent or component would otherwise center text. Do not add `text-center` to content blocks unless Diana explicitly requests it.
- Keep button labels centered within their controls and numeric totals aligned for readability where appropriate.
- Apply this rule when editing existing areas without broadly restyling unrelated pages.
- Example: cart payment helper text above the action row uses `text-left`, aligned with the subtotal label and form fields.
